    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759-a6">

                <pb facs="0917" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg823"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No.
                    2756.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pulido to Mr.
                            Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Superior Court of Habana,<lb/>Office of the
                                Presidency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-01-14"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 14,
                    1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your attentive communication of the 13th instant, in which you ask to be
                    informed of the facts and of the law upon which the indictment and commitment to
                    prison of the American citizen, Mr. Julio Sanguily y Garit, are founded,
                    manifesting to you at the same time that I have ordered a copy of your said
                    communication to be sent to the third section of the hall for the trial of
                    criminal cases of this superior court for its action in the matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">José Pulido.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
